  "query_preview": "from wrn NV to srn CA. These showers/storms will \ncontinue to move to the east-northeast this morning and \ngradually decrease in areal coverage as the morning progresses. \nSatellite imagery this morning showed clearer skies across \nsouthwest Arizona. So expect partly cloudy skies once the \nshowers end and then see scattered redevelopment of low-topped \nshowers/storms with the afternoon heating and the dynamics \nassociated with the above mentioned trof. Can't rule out a \nfrisky storm or two producing very small hail with the cool \nsummer mid-level 500 mb temps of -6C.\n\nDrier does filters in across the area tomorrow and continuing\ninto this weekend. Still enough moisture around for a chance of\nafternoon/evening storms mainly south and east of Tucson. The\nonce caveat to this is the potential for an easterly wave, which\nis currently along the Mexican coast of the GoA, moving across \nnorthern Mexico on Sunday. Something to keep an eye one as this\nmay bring a better chance of storms that what is currently in\nthe forecast.\n\nTemperatures will be below normal today, then warm up again to \nabove normal this weekend into next week with moderate to\nlocalized Major HeatRisk and triple digit highs returning to\nmost of the area.",
